  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "aa86b9c7-7f41-42fd-b68e-48ce77a16811",
      "name": "Panel: WORKFLOW DETAILS",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 460,
        "height": 1200,
        "content": "## \ud83d\udcd8 WORKFLOW DETAILS\n\n**Motorsports Tech Inspection Pass/Fail Router**\nScores every safety-equipment item's expiry against its rating-specific cycle, then routes the whole car into one of four inspection outcomes automatically.\n\n**Who it's for:** SCCA/NASA-style club racing tech inspectors and chief stewards who need consistent, fast pass/conditional/fail/DQ decisions at trackside.\n\n**Execution walkthrough**\n1. Trackside tech-inspection app POSTs one car's submission (driver/car info + safety-equipment array) to the webhook.\n2. Equipment array is split out; each item is deterministically scored for days-to-expiry against its class's expiry cycle (helmet 5yr, harness 2yr, etc.), in parallel with a class-metadata tag.\n3. Branches merge and aggregate into one consolidated equipment-compliance score for the car.\n4. Text Classifier reads the aggregated score plus inspector notes and routes to Pass / Conditional-Pass-Rework / Fail / Disqualify.\n5. Each of the 4 classifier outputs is stamped onto a `inspectionCategory` field by its own Set node (Text Classifier itself never writes a field).\n6. A 4-way Switch reads that field and drives 4 genuinely different terminal actions, with a nested If on the Pass path checking the grid-position eligibility cutoff time.\n7. Every terminal action posts to the race-control timing API, archives to Google Sheets, and (for DQ) escalates to the chief steward on Slack before a final crew-channel notification.\n\n**Node-by-node summary**\n\n| Node | Role |\n|---|---|\n| Receive Car Inspection Submission | Webhook trigger |\n| Split Equipment Line Items | Fan-out per equipment item |\n| Compute Item Expiry & Pass Fail | Code: real expiry logic |\n| Merge / Aggregate | Fan-in + compliance score |\n| Classify Overall Inspection Result | AI: Text Classifier (4-way) |\n| Tag *Category (x4) | Per-branch field stamps |\n| Route By Inspection Category | 4-way Switch |\n| Check Grid Eligibility Cutoff Time | Nested If (secondary check) |\n| HTTP Request (x4) | Primary sink: race-control API |\n| Log Inspection Result Archive | Google Sheets archival log |\n| Slack (x2) | Crew notify + chief-steward escalation |\n\n**Expected input:** webhook POST (driver/car info + equipment array with dates/ratings).\n**Expected output:** one race-control API post + one archive row per car; DQ additionally pings the chief steward.\n\n**Sticky colour legend:** trigger=1, transform=2, ai=3, branch=4, storage=5, notify=6.\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "649ed52d-6f99-4a72-84d0-265c7858ac12",
      "name": "Panel: SETUP GUIDE",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        1560
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 6,
        "width": 460,
        "height": 660,
        "content": "## \u2699\ufe0f SETUP GUIDE\n\n1. Import this JSON via n8n -> Workflows -> Import from File.\n2. Create/attach credentials:\n   - **OpenAI Account - Tech Inspection Classifier** on *Inspection Classification Model*.\n   - **Race Control Timing API - Header Auth** (HTTP Header Auth) on all 4 HTTP Request nodes.\n   - **Google Sheets Account - Tech Inspection Archive** on *Log Inspection Result Archive*.\n   - **Slack Account - Chief Steward Escalation** on *Escalate Disqualification To Chief Steward*.\n   - **Slack Account - Tech Inspection Crew** on *Notify Tech Inspection Crew Channel*.\n3. Set the webhook path on *Receive Car Inspection Submission* to match your trackside app's configured endpoint (default `tech-inspection-submission`).\n4. Replace `PLACEHOLDER_SHEET_ID` on the archive node, and the two `PLACEHOLDER_*_CHANNEL` Slack channel IDs.\n5. Point all 4 HTTP Request nodes at your real race-control/timing-system URL (replace the internal.example.com mock).\n6. Tune the expiry cycles (`cycles` map) inside *Compute Item Expiry & Pass Fail* to your sanctioning body's actual rules if they differ from the SCCA/NASA defaults used here.\n7. **To test:** POST a sample car with one expired harness to confirm it lands in Fail, and one with all-valid equipment to confirm it lands in Pass and respects the grid cutoff check.\n8. **Estimated setup time:** 25-35 minutes (5 credentials + webhook path + 3 placeholder values).\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ac571c52-3426-4f30-b9c0-b2a88699fbcb",
      "name": "Panel: CUSTOMISATION",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        2280
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 460,
        "height": 420,
        "content": "## \ud83c\udfa8 CUSTOMISATION\n\n1. **Add a 5th category (e.g. \"Provisional\"):** extend the categories list on *Classify Overall Inspection Result*, add a matching Set-tag node, and a 5th Switch output.\n2. **Per-class cutoff windows:** give each equipment class its own grid-eligibility cutoff instead of one shared value used by *Check Grid Eligibility Cutoff Time*.\n3. **Auto-schedule reinspection:** wire *Post Rework Deadline & Reinspection Slot*'s response into a Google Calendar node to book the actual reinspection slot.\n4. **Point-standings integration:** add a second HTTP Request off *Post Disqualification Escalation* to notify a championship points-tracking system.\n5. **Multi-series support:** parameterize the expiry `cycles` map per racing series if you run more than one sanctioning body's tech rules through this workflow.\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "91dcc538-c9ff-406f-9666-fb439700cddd",
      "name": "Panel: ADDITIONAL INFORMATION",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        2760
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 460,
        "height": 560,
        "content": "## \u2139\ufe0f ADDITIONAL INFORMATION\n\n**Error handling:** every external-call node (Text Classifier + its Chat Model, all HTTP Requests, both Slack nodes, Google Sheets) retries up to 3 times with a 2s wait and continues on final failure rather than blocking grid formation.\n\n**API cost/rate-limits:** 1 OpenAI classification call per car submission; 1-2 HTTP posts and 1-2 Slack messages per car depending on category.\n\n**Data privacy:** driver name, car number, and inspector notes are sent to OpenAI for classification - avoid putting unrelated personal data in the notes field.\n\n**n8n version:** unknown - built to current stable as of 2026-09-25, offline-verified node types - re-check on first import.\n\n**Known limitations:** the grid-eligibility cutoff time is read from the submission payload (`gridEligibilityCutoff`); your trackside app must supply it per event.\n\n**Creator credit:** Swapnil AI Labs - swapnil.mandloi7@gmail.com - swapnilailabs.netlify.app\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
